1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,528
If this video found you, your life is about to change.

2
00:00:05,078 --> 00:00:06,518
Is this you lately?

3
00:00:06,718 --> 00:00:11,218
When your phone buzzes, you're tired before you even open it.

4
00:00:11,418 --> 00:00:16,169
When someone cancels plans, you feel, guiltily, relieved.

5
00:00:16,369 --> 00:00:20,906
The gatherings that used to be so fun now feel strangely empty.

6
00:00:21,455 --> 00:00:24,083
And being alone feels more and more comfortable.

7
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:27,225
Have you been worried that something's wrong with you?

8
00:00:27,426 --> 00:00:28,362
There isn't.

9
00:00:28,561 --> 00:00:33,385
This is a season many people pass through, right before their life changes in a big way.

10
00:00:33,936 --> 00:00:38,436
Today, I'll talk about why this season comes, and how to move through it.

11
00:00:38,636 --> 00:00:43,640
And at the end, I'll tell you the story of the caterpillar in the cocoon.

12
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:47,274
First, we need to separate two things.

13
00:00:47,474 --> 00:00:50,426
Loneliness and solitude are not the same.

14
00:00:50,976 --> 00:00:53,892
The theologian Paul Tillich put it like this.

15
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:57,332
Loneliness is the word for the pain of being alone.

16
00:00:57,532 --> 00:01:01,708
Solitude is the word for the glory of being alone.

17
00:01:02,258 --> 00:01:07,118
You can be just as alone, but loneliness is a state of having lost yourself.

18
00:01:07,318 --> 00:01:09,226
You wait for someone to fill you.

19
00:01:09,426 --> 00:01:12,954
Solitude is a state of having come back to yourself.

20
00:01:13,154 --> 00:01:16,610
No one is there, and yet you feel full.

21
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:22,271
The aloneness that feels comfortable to you right now is probably solitude.

22
00:01:23,422 --> 00:01:25,726
So why does a season like this come?

23
00:01:25,926 --> 00:01:27,690
There are four reasons.

24
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,904
First, because you've outgrown your shell.

25
00:01:31,104 --> 00:01:35,604
As a lobster grows, its hard shell starts to squeeze, and it hurts.

26
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:39,692
So it hides under a rock and sheds the shell.

27
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:45,220
Then it waits, alone, until the new one hardens.

28
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:49,236
The discomfort you feel now is a sign that you've grown.

29
00:01:49,786 --> 00:01:53,206
Second, because your energy has changed.

30
00:01:53,406 --> 00:02:00,786
When your frequency shifts, you no longer resonate with the old people, the old conversations, the old fun.

31
00:02:00,986 --> 00:02:02,858
No one did anything wrong.

32
00:02:03,058 --> 00:02:05,110
It just doesn't fit anymore.

33
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:09,764
Third, because you have to empty before you can be filled.

34
00:02:09,964 --> 00:02:16,984
A cup full of other people's expectations and the world's noise has no room for anything new.

35
00:02:17,184 --> 00:02:20,172
Time alone is time to empty that cup.

36
00:02:20,722 --> 00:02:24,466
Fourth, because your luck is changing seasons.

37
00:02:24,666 --> 00:02:33,594
In Korean saju, the Four Pillars of Destiny, it's said that this happens often when a great cycle of fortune turns, when new luck is opening.

38
00:02:33,794 --> 00:02:38,546
People fall away, you want to be alone, and the old ways stop fitting.

39
00:02:38,746 --> 00:02:45,334
Just as your body feels off when the seasons change, your heart and relationships shake when your fortune changes.

40
00:02:45,534 --> 00:02:50,286
Spiritual traditions call this the time right before a great awakening.

41
00:02:51,436 --> 00:02:55,864
Of course, right now it may feel awkward, uncomfortable, even frightening.

42
00:02:56,064 --> 00:02:58,620
You don't have to force yourself to be happy about it.

43
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:02,456
That feeling is valid, just as it is.

44
00:03:03,006 --> 00:03:04,986
But you're not falling apart.

45
00:03:05,186 --> 00:03:11,270
These are growing pains, from a process of growing in every part of your life and rising to a higher level.

46
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:19,236
Pascal once wrote: all of humanity's problems stem from man's inability to sit quietly in a room alone.

47
00:03:19,786 --> 00:03:24,718
Maybe that's why great awakenings have always been preceded by solitude.

48
00:03:24,918 --> 00:03:26,718
Forty days in the wilderness.

49
00:03:26,918 --> 00:03:29,402
The Buddha sitting alone beneath the Bodhi tree.

50
00:03:29,602 --> 00:03:32,230
Countless meditators in mountain caves.

51
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:35,552
In game terms, this is a save point.

52
00:03:35,752 --> 00:03:40,072
A place to stop and rest before the next stage.

53
00:03:40,272 --> 00:03:43,692
Time to log out of someone else's game, just for a while.

54
00:03:44,842 --> 00:03:48,478
And now, the most important thing about this season.

55
00:03:49,028 --> 00:03:54,788
You, whoever you are, never came to Earth to take care of someone else.

56
00:03:54,988 --> 00:03:58,552
You never came to please anyone, or to satisfy anyone.

57
00:03:59,102 --> 00:04:02,306
We came to keep discovering what our soul wants.

58
00:04:02,506 --> 00:04:05,566
To remember ourselves, and to remember us.

59
00:04:05,766 --> 00:04:13,182
To have a body, and among all the experiences only Earth can offer, to choose and live more of the ones our soul wants.

60
00:04:13,732 --> 00:04:16,684
So in this season, be more selfish.

61
00:04:17,234 --> 00:04:20,114
Selfish doesn't mean hurting others.

62
00:04:20,314 --> 00:04:22,798
It means filling yourself first.

63
00:04:22,998 --> 00:04:27,750
On a plane, they tell you to put on your own oxygen mask first.

64
00:04:27,950 --> 00:04:31,586
You have to breathe before you can help the person next to you.

65
00:04:31,786 --> 00:04:34,666
An empty pitcher can't pour for anyone.

66
00:04:35,216 --> 00:04:40,076
Speak, think, and act by how your soul feels.

67
00:04:40,276 --> 00:04:44,488
Say what your heart wants to say, not what others want to hear.

68
00:04:44,688 --> 00:04:50,772
Instead of asking how others will see you, ask first: how does my soul feel right now?

69
00:04:50,972 --> 00:04:55,112
Choose what makes your soul lighter, over what you're supposed to do.

70
00:04:55,662 --> 00:04:59,766
That doesn't mean caring for and loving others is wrong.

71
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:10,190
Raising a child, caring for someone who's sick, a job that looks to everyone else like enormous sacrifice and service, that might be exactly the experience your soul wants.

72
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:14,916
If so, do it, no matter what anyone says.

73
00:05:15,466 --> 00:05:19,570
What matters isn't what you do, but why you do it.

74
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:24,630
What you do to satisfy others, to be a good person, empties you.

75
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:30,482
But what you do because your soul wants it, however much it looks like sacrifice, fills you.

76
00:05:31,032 --> 00:05:32,472
And accept everything.

77
00:05:32,671 --> 00:05:37,099
The time alone, the people leaving, the discomfort right now.

78
00:05:37,299 --> 00:05:39,639
In the end, we are all that is.

79
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:43,224
Everything simply exists, and everything is energy.

80
00:05:43,424 --> 00:05:46,556
In truth, right and wrong don't exist.

81
00:05:46,756 --> 00:05:48,664
They're just names we gave things.

82
00:05:48,864 --> 00:05:52,284
So there's no reason to fit yourself to anyone else's standard.

83
00:05:53,434 --> 00:05:55,198
So what should you do in this season?

84
00:05:55,398 --> 00:05:57,486
Just remember seven things.

85
00:05:58,036 --> 00:06:00,916
One, be selfish without guilt.

86
00:06:01,116 --> 00:06:06,551
When you turn down plans, you can say: today, I have plans with myself.

87
00:06:07,102 --> 00:06:09,982
Two, take care of your body first.

88
00:06:10,181 --> 00:06:13,385
Sleep enough, walk, eat something warm.

89
00:06:13,585 --> 00:06:17,114
When your soul is changing, your body needs rest too.

90
00:06:17,663 --> 00:06:19,859
Three, empty out.

91
00:06:20,059 --> 00:06:26,647
Tidy your room, let go of clothes you don't wear, and unfollow the accounts that make you uneasy every time you see them.

92
00:06:26,847 --> 00:06:29,619
New energy comes in when there's space.

93
00:06:30,169 --> 00:06:32,402
Four, stop comparing.

94
00:06:32,602 --> 00:06:35,770
This isn't the time to watch other people's pace.

95
00:06:35,969 --> 00:06:40,073
Inside the cocoon, you don't need to look at anyone else's wings.

96
00:06:40,623 --> 00:06:43,179
Five, follow small pulls.

97
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:49,464
A book, a place, a song you're drawn to for no reason, that's your soul giving directions.

98
00:06:50,014 --> 00:06:51,454
Six, write.

99
00:06:51,654 --> 00:06:53,850
Before bed, just one line.

100
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:56,354
What did I truly want today?

101
00:06:56,554 --> 00:06:57,418
Who am I?

102
00:06:57,968 --> 00:07:01,640
Seven, don't rush big decisions.

103
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:08,248
Quitting, breaking up, moving, make those choices in stillness, not on impulse.

104
00:07:08,448 --> 00:07:11,724
In this season, the answers become clear slowly.

105
00:07:12,874 --> 00:07:16,438
So let's take one minute together, right now.

106
00:07:16,988 --> 00:07:19,544
Sit comfortably and close your eyes.

107
00:07:19,744 --> 00:07:23,920
Breathe in slowly… and breathe out, long.

108
00:07:24,470 --> 00:07:27,890
Right now, in this moment, you're alone.

109
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:29,170
And that's okay.

110
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:33,248
Quietly ask: what do I truly want?

111
00:07:33,798 --> 00:07:34,842
And once more.

112
00:07:35,042 --> 00:07:35,906
Who am I?

113
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:38,544
It's okay if no answer comes.

114
00:07:38,744 --> 00:07:42,848
Just by asking, your soul takes one step closer to you.

115
00:07:43,398 --> 00:07:49,302
Now, take a deep breath in… and as you slowly breathe out, open your eyes.

116
00:07:50,452 --> 00:07:53,800
Now, here's the cocoon story I promised.

117
00:07:54,350 --> 00:07:59,282
Before a caterpillar becomes a butterfly, it goes into a cocoon on its own.

118
00:07:59,482 --> 00:08:03,370
Inside, it's dark and tight, and no one is there.

119
00:08:03,570 --> 00:08:06,162
But that's exactly where the wings are made.

120
00:08:06,712 --> 00:08:11,140
So if being alone has become comfortable, you haven't lost your way.

121
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:13,032
You're coming back to yourself.

122
00:08:13,582 --> 00:08:15,562
You didn't come here to please anyone.

123
00:08:15,762 --> 00:08:17,634
Be a little more selfish.

124
00:08:17,834 --> 00:08:23,918
Take care of yourself, love yourself, and choose the experiences your soul wants.

125
00:08:24,118 --> 00:08:28,798
And keep going, remembering who you are, and who we are.

126
00:08:29,348 --> 00:08:38,816
But if all your joy has disappeared and you can't do anything for a long time, that may not be solitude, but a sign that you need support.

127
00:08:39,016 --> 00:08:43,192
The numbers in the description connect you with someone who will listen.

128
00:08:43,742 --> 00:08:47,378
Tell me in the comments one reason you need time alone right now.

129
00:08:47,928 --> 00:08:49,116
Play your own game.
